From 1045a031d1489711858e6b5168eeb1e1d41ab964 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:42:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] edid: expose structured extension parsing failures

The global diagnostic string mixes descriptive base-block warnings with
extension ambiguity. A consumer rejecting that whole string cannot use
valid native DisplayID data on the ROG panel, whose base range/timing
warnings do not affect interpretation of its extension blocks.

Track extension failure state independently of logger formatting. Include
extension diagnostics, every discarded/uninterpretable extension, checksum
failures before early drops, and all input-size/block-count mismatches.
Keep base header/version/checksum rejection and diagnostic text unchanged.
The additive query reports known failures, not full conformance or readiness.

Public-API tests cover unrelated base warnings, ordinary/nested extension
failures, silently dropped unsupported versions, checksum/drop paths,
revision-conditioned unknown tags, all framing mismatches and fatal base
checks. Compiler and sanitizer qualification follows source review.
